USOS 3.1.2-usos1 patch 3/3: no boot menu prompt or wait on a quiet boot

csm_maininit adds the romfiles etc/show-boot-menu=0 and etc/boot-menu-wait=0
(next to etc/extra-pci-roots) when csm_quiet(), so interactive_bootmenu
returns at once: no "Press ESC for boot menu." and no 2.5 s wait.

Applies to CSMWrap 3.1.2 (808ac8e) with its seabios submodule (578d260b),
patch -p1 from the top of the tree. Part of CSMWrap 3.1.2-usos1, a MODIFIED
version made by the USOS project (LGPL-2.1 / SeaBIOS LGPLv3).

diff -ruN a/seabios/src/fw/csm.c b/seabios/src/fw/csm.c
--- a/seabios/src/fw/csm.c
+++ b/seabios/src/fw/csm.c
@@ -90,6 +90,11 @@
                               (void *)csm_compat_table.ExtraPciRootListPointer,
                               csm_compat_table.ExtraPciRootListCount);
     }
+    // Quiet boot: no "Press ESC for boot menu" prompt and no wait.
+    if (csm_quiet()) {
+        const_romfile_add_int("etc/show-boot-menu", 0);
+        const_romfile_add_int("etc/boot-menu-wait", 0);
+    }
     pci_probe_devices();
 
     csm_compat_table.PnPInstallationCheckSegment = SEG_BIOS;
